# a textured word — Content Slot Map

**Companion to:** `a-textured-word-master-web-brief.md`
**Purpose:** every slot on the site, in build order, with the placeholder text that goes into the staging build until real content replaces it.

---

## How this document works

Each slot has an ID, a literal placeholder, a limit, an owner and a fallback.

- **OWNER: ANEESA** — copy or asset she supplies. Nothing gets written for her.
- **OWNER: DEV** — structural, already decided in the brief, no input needed.
- **OWNER: DRAFT EXISTS** — the facts are already in her discovery notes. She confirms or corrects the wording. She does not start from blank.

**The placeholder goes into the build exactly as written**, in mono, `--clay-ink` on `--paper-lift`, so that a walkthrough of the staging site is also the content checklist. Nothing ships with lorem ipsum.

**Limits are not suggestions.** They come from the type scale in §3.3 of the brief. Copy over the limit breaks the layout and creates a revision round.

**Fallback** is what happens if the slot is empty at the agreed content deadline. Fallbacks are how the site launches on time. Agree the deadline in writing before build starts.

